# solid_sdd

This project uses solid_sdd for machine-checkable Spec-Driven Development.
Skills are installed via `gh skill` (typically under `.agents/skills/solidsdd-*`).

## Contract artifacts (defaults)

- OpenAPI: `openapi/openapi.yaml`
- OCL: `contracts/**/*.ocl`
- Derived contract tests: `tests/contracts/**/*.test.ts` (dependents of OCL; not source of truth)

## Adapters

- API: OpenAPI 3.x — see `solidsdd-apply-api/references/openapi-adapter.md` (or sibling install path)
- DbC: UML OCL → contract tests via `solidsdd-derive-tests` — see `solidsdd-apply-dbc/references/ocl-adapter.md`
- Formal specs (TLA+ / Alloy / …): defer with rationale when relevant (MVP)

## Verification

- Do not treat work as done if OpenAPI checks or OCL-derived contract tests fail
- On failure, return to the suggested skill; do not weaken contracts to force a pass

## Execution (orchestrator / subagent)

- `solidsdd-loop` is parent-only
- From an orchestrator, run `solidsdd-judge`, `solidsdd-apply-api`, `solidsdd-apply-dbc`, `solidsdd-derive-tests`, `solidsdd-implement`, and `solidsdd-verify` as **explicit Task subagents** — never inline in the parent
- Do not thin or rewrite `ApplicationPlan` in the parent; re-run `solidsdd-judge` as a subagent if needed
- Details: `solidsdd-loop/references/execution-model.md`
